Package: panasonic-fz-g1-support
Architecture: all
Depends: convertible-helper (>= 1.1.0), kmod, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Panasonic Toughpad FZ-G1 hardware support for Debian
 Settings that make the brightness control of a Panasonic Toughpad FZ-G1
 (first generation) work from the GNOME settings panel on Debian: it makes
 sure the panasonic_laptop module is loaded (a leftover blacklist file for it
 is moved aside), and re-writes the Panasonic brightness register once at
 boot. When the keyboard dock is detached it counts as tablet mode
 (through convertible-helper), so GNOME raises its full on-screen keyboard.
 .
 The files are applied only when the DMI product name begins with FZ-G1.
